node_modules/
dist/
coverage/

# Secrets and runtime state. None of these belongs in git, and the `.example`
# files are the committed templates.
#
# `members.json` (legacy) and `member-store.json` hold member token digests;
# `invite-store.json` holds the digests of invites that have not been redeemed
# yet, which are live credentials until they are; `quota-store.json` holds who
# spent what. This repository is public and a self-hoster runs from a clone of
# it, so an un-ignored state file is a credential in somebody's fork.
.env*
!.env.example
members.json
member-store.json
invite-store.json
quota-store.json
audit-log.jsonl
*.log

# Agent scratch. Internal working notes and transient worktrees, not project
# documentation, and this repository is public.
.claude/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
